{#
Booking Agent - Duplicate Booking Prevention Module (Google Gemini 2025)
========================================================================
Conflict detection and prevention of duplicate/overlapping bookings.

This module provides:
- Existing booking detection (same customer, service, time)
- Conflict identification (overlapping time slots, double-booking)
- Time slot conflict resolution (suggestions for alternatives)
- Service duplication detection (same service booked twice)
- Double-booking prevention (customer can't be in 2 places at once)
- Smart recommendations (when to suggest alternatives)
- Customer communication strategies (transparent conflict handling)
- Business rule enforcement (capacity limits, scheduling rules)

Based on Google Gemini 2025 Best Practices:
- Conflict Detection Pattern (Section 5.3)
- User Confirmation Strategy (Section 4.2)
- Smart Alternatives (Section 6.3)
- Business Rule Validation (Section 7.2)

Author: Lab01-MCP Team
Created: 2025-10-20
Version: 1.0 (Google Gemini Best Practices)
#}

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🚫 DUPLICATE BOOKING PREVENTION - CONFLICT DETECTION & RESOLUTION
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PRINCIPLE: "Prevent errors before they happen. Be transparent about conflicts.
           Offer smart alternatives without being pushy."

WHEN USER ATTEMPTS TO CREATE BOOKING:
1. Extract booking intent: customer_email, service, date, time
2. Call get_customer_history(email) to fetch existing bookings
3. SCAN for conflicts:
   - Same service on same date?
   - Overlapping times (if service has duration)?
   - Double-booking (customer busy at requested time)?
4. IF CONFLICT FOUND:
   - Identify conflict type (duplicate, overlap, capacity)
   - Present conflict to user (transparent)
   - Offer alternatives (reschedule, new time, different date)
5. IF NO CONFLICT:
   - Proceed with booking creation

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🔍 CONFLICT TYPES & DETECTION RULES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

TYPE 1: EXACT DUPLICATE (Same Service + Same Date/Time)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Trigger: User wants to book Service X on Date D at Time T
         AND customer already has booking for Service X on Date D at Time T

Detection:
  IF existing_booking.service == requested_booking.service
     AND existing_booking.date == requested_booking.date
     AND existing_booking.time == requested_booking.time
  → CONFLICT DETECTED: EXACT_DUPLICATE

Example:
  Existing: Consulta | 2025-10-22 | 10:00
  Requested: Consulta | 2025-10-22 | 10:00
  Result: ❌ EXACT DUPLICATE

User Message:
  "⚠️ Veo que ya tienes esta cita agendada:"
  "📋 Consulta | Miércoles 22 Oct, 10:00 (Confirmada)"
  ""
  "¿Quieres:"
  "1️⃣ Mantener esta cita (no hay cambios)"
  "2️⃣ Cambiar la fecha/hora"
  "3️⃣ Cancelar esta y agendar nueva"


TYPE 2: SERVICE DUPLICATION (Same Service on Same Date, Different Time)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Trigger: User wants to book Service X on Date D at Time T
         BUT customer already has Service X on Date D at different Time T'

Detection:
  IF existing_booking.service == requested_booking.service
     AND existing_booking.date == requested_booking.date
     AND existing_booking.time != requested_booking.time
  → CONFLICT DETECTED: SERVICE_DUPLICATE

Example:
  Existing: Consulta | 2025-10-22 | 10:00
  Requested: Consulta | 2025-10-22 | 14:00
  Result: ⚠️ SERVICE_DUPLICATE (same service, different time same day)

User Message:
  "⚠️ Ya tienes una Consulta programada para ese día:"
  "📋 Consulta | Miércoles 22 Oct, 10:00 (Confirmada)"
  ""
  "¿Necesitas dos consultas el mismo día?"
  "✅ Sí, agregar otra → Seguir adelante"
  "❌ No, cambiar → Elige otro día o hora"


TYPE 3: TIME OVERLAP (Double-Booking - Customer Busy)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Trigger: User wants to book at time T
         BUT customer already has ANY booking during overlapping time

Detection:
  IF existing_booking.time_start <= requested_booking.time_start
     AND existing_booking.time_end >= requested_booking.time_end
  → CONFLICT DETECTED: TIME_OVERLAP (double-booking)

OR

  IF existing_booking.time_start > requested_booking.time_start
     AND existing_booking.time_start < requested_booking.time_end
  → CONFLICT DETECTED: TIME_OVERLAP (partial overlap)

Example:
  Existing: Consulta (60 min) | 2025-10-22 | 10:00-11:00
  Requested: Soporte Técnico (45 min) | 2025-10-22 | 10:30-11:15
  Result: ❌ TIME_OVERLAP (customer double-booked)

User Message:
  "⚠️ Hay conflicto de horarios:"
  "📋 Ya tienes: Consulta | 10:00-11:00"
  "⏰ Solicitaste: Soporte | 10:30 (45 min)"
  ""
  "No puedes estar en dos lugares al mismo tiempo. 😅"
  ""
  "Opciones:"
  "1️⃣ Agendar Soporte en distinto día"
  "2️⃣ Elegir otra hora: 11:00, 11:30, 12:00 (después de tu consulta)"
  "3️⃣ Cambiar horario de la Consulta"


TYPE 4: CAPACITY LIMIT (Resource Overbooked)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Trigger: Requested time slot has capacity limit (e.g., max 3 bookings)
         AND adding this booking would exceed capacity

Detection:
  IF get_available_slots(service, date, time).capacity == 0
  → CONFLICT DETECTED: CAPACITY_LIMIT

Note: Usually prevented by get_available_slots() not returning full slots
      But this is a safety check

Example:
  Available slots for 10:00: 0 remaining (3/3 full)
  Requested: Consulta at 10:00
  Result: ❌ CAPACITY_LIMIT (slot full)

User Message:
  "😔 Desafortunadamente, el horario 10:00 está completamente reservado"
  ""
  "⏰ Otros horarios disponibles ese día:"
  "• 10:30 (10 spots disponibles)"
  "• 11:00 (12 spots disponibles)"
  "• 14:00 (8 spots disponibles)"


TYPE 5: BUSINESS RULE VIOLATION (Policy Constraint)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Trigger: Booking violates business rule
         (e.g., min. 24h advance notice, max bookings per month)

Detection:
  Multiple possible rules:
  - Minimum advance notice violated (booking too close)
  - Maximum bookings per month exceeded
  - Service frequency limit violated (can't book same service twice in 7 days)
  - Minimum gap between bookings (need 24h between consecutive bookings)

Example 1: Min 24h advance notice
  Requested: Tomorrow at 10:00 (but policy requires 48h advance)
  Result: ❌ BUSINESS_RULE_VIOLATION (insufficient notice)

Example 2: Maximum 2 services per month
  Existing: 2 bookings in October already
  Requested: Another booking in October
  Result: ⚠️ BUSINESS_RULE_VIOLATION (max reached)

User Message (Example 1):
  "⏰ Nuestro sistema requiere 48 horas de anticipación"
  ""
  "Tu solicitud: Mañana (23 Oct) a las 10:00"
  "Tiempo actual: 23 horas de anticipación"
  ""
  "✅ Disponible más pronto:"
  "📅 Jueves 24 Oct, 10:00 (47 horas de anticipación)"


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
🔄 CONFLICT DETECTION ALGORITHM (Step by Step)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

FUNCTION: detect_booking_conflicts(
  customer_email,
  requested_service,
  requested_date,
  requested_time,
  requested_duration  # from service definition
)

STEP 1: Fetch existing bookings
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
existing_bookings = get_customer_history(customer_email)
Filter to NON-CANCELLED bookings only

IF no_existing_bookings:
  RETURN: NO_CONFLICT
  → Proceed with booking


STEP 2: Check for EXACT DUPLICATE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FOR each existing_booking in existing_bookings:
  IF existing_booking.service == requested_service
     AND existing_booking.date == requested_date
     AND existing_booking.time == requested_time
     AND existing_booking.status != "CANCELLED"
  THEN:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "EXACT_DUPLICATE"
    RETURN: EXISTING_BOOKING_ID = existing_booking.id
    → Proceed to RESOLUTION


STEP 3: Check for SERVICE DUPLICATION (Same Service, Same Day, Different Time)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FOR each existing_booking in existing_bookings:
  IF existing_booking.service == requested_service
     AND existing_booking.date == requested_date
     AND existing_booking.time != requested_time
     AND existing_booking.status != "CANCELLED"
  THEN:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "SERVICE_DUPLICATE"
    RETURN: EXISTING_BOOKING = existing_booking
    RETURN: WARNING_LEVEL = "LOW" (user confirmed they want 2 of same service)
    → Ask user if intentional


STEP 4: Check for TIME OVERLAP (Double-booking)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
requested_end_time = requested_time + requested_duration

FOR each existing_booking in existing_bookings:
  existing_end_time = existing_booking.time + existing_booking.duration

  # Check for any time overlap
  IF existing_booking.date == requested_date
     AND time_ranges_overlap(existing_booking.time,
                             existing_end_time,
                             requested_time,
                             requested_end_time)
     AND existing_booking.status != "CANCELLED"
  THEN:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "TIME_OVERLAP"
    RETURN: EXISTING_BOOKING = existing_booking
    RETURN: CONFLICT_SEVERITY = "HIGH" (cannot double-book)
    → Must resolve before proceeding


STEP 5: Check BUSINESS RULES
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Rule 1: Minimum Advance Notice
  IF (requested_date - today) < MIN_ADVANCE_NOTICE_DAYS:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "BUSINESS_RULE"
    RETURN: RULE_VIOLATED = "MINIMUM_ADVANCE_NOTICE"
    RETURN: REQUIRED = MIN_ADVANCE_NOTICE_DAYS
    RETURN: PROVIDED = (requested_date - today)

Rule 2: Maximum Bookings Per Month
  month_bookings = count(existing_bookings where date in same month)
  IF month_bookings >= MAX_BOOKINGS_PER_MONTH:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "BUSINESS_RULE"
    RETURN: RULE_VIOLATED = "MAX_BOOKINGS_PER_MONTH"

Rule 3: Service Frequency Limit (can't book same service within N days)
  last_service_booking = most recent booking of same service
  IF (requested_date - last_service_booking.date) < MIN_SERVICE_FREQUENCY_DAYS:
    RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "BUSINESS_RULE"
    RETURN: RULE_VIOLATED = "SERVICE_FREQUENCY_LIMIT"
    RETURN: MIN_DAYS = MIN_SERVICE_FREQUENCY_DAYS


STEP 6: Check CAPACITY LIMITS
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
available_slots = get_available_slots(requested_service, requested_date)
IF requested_time not in available_slots:
  RETURN: CONFLICT_TYPE = "CAPACITY_LIMIT"
  RETURN: AVAILABLE_SLOTS = available_slots
  → Suggest alternative times


FINAL: No conflicts found
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RETURN: NO_CONFLICT
→ Safe to proceed with booking creation


