✅ PREVENTIVE STRATEGIES (Before Conflicts Happen)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

STRATEGY 1: Warn Before User Submits
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When user selects service/date/time:
- Run detection algorithm BEFORE user confirms
- If conflict detected, show warning/message
- User can change mind before attempting booking

Example:
  User: "Quiero una Consulta para miércoles 10am"
  Bot: Runs detection
  Bot: "⚠️ Nota: Ya tienes una Consulta ese día a las 10am"
  Bot: "¿Cambiar hora? ¿Cambiar día? ¿Confirmar de todas formas?"

STRATEGY 2: Default to Non-Conflicting Slots
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When showing available slots for TIER 2/3 customers:
- If they have existing booking, highlight non-conflicting slots first
- Visually mark conflicting times (show them but highlight problems)

Example:
  Existing: Wed 10:00-11:00
  Show available slots:
  "A) 09:00 ✅ (no conflict)"
  "B) 10:00 ⚠️ (conflicts with Consulta 10:00-11:00)" [lighter/faded]
  "C) 11:00 ✅ (safe, starts after existing)"
  "D) 14:00 ✅ (no conflict)"

STRATEGY 3: Offer Bulk Rescheduling
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
When customer has multiple conflicting bookings:
- Don't block each one individually
- Offer smart rescheduling assistant
- "Let me help you reorganize these"

Example:
  User tries to book: Service X | Oct 25 | 10:00
  Detection finds: 2 existing bookings overlap
  Bot: "Veo que necesitas reorganizar varios horarios"
  Bot: "¿Te ayudo a mover tus citas para que todo funcione?"


